On Sun, Jun 13, 2010 at 7:50 AM, Pierre Abbat <phma@phma.optus.nu> wrote:

> I found [[kerlo]] on Wikipedia, which needs some work. The word "mrubo'u"
> is
> obvious, but what do we call anvils and stirrups, either in the ordinary
> sense, or in the ear bone sense?
>
> Pierre
> --'


 An anvil in the "ordinary sense" is already in jbovlaste as jimda'izbe .
 For the earbone, I'd suggest the jargon term "kerzbebo'u".  As for stirrup,
I'd say xirtizyclupa for the ordinary sense, and kercupybo'u for the ear
sense.

      --gejyspa

